  "Id": 1386,
  "Title": "AKU Convocation 2011: Uganda",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "The Advanced Nursing School in Kampala, Uganda graduated 49 students. Twenty-nine students received a Bachelor of Science in Nursing and 20 students were awarded a Diploma in General Nursing.",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<div class=\"ExternalClass9555ABCD9AE14A4B9A7BE29E41FE0ECA\"><p>\u200bThe Advanced Nursing School in Kampala, Uganda graduated 49 students. Twenty-nine students received a Bachelor of Science in Nursing and 20 students were awarded a Diploma in General Nursing. An award of academic excellence was presented to Junit Annete Wakore, who graduated with a Bachelor of Science degree in Nursing and Susan Alum who graduated with a Diploma in General Nursing.<br><br>This award was presented to them for having demonstrated outstanding performance in their studies.<br><br>Professor George Wilson Kanyeihamba, Former Supreme Court Judge and Legal Advisor on Human Rights and International Affairs to President Museveni of Uganda, was the chief guest.\u200b \u200b</p></div>",
